From a3d1737680183f64242e22a8e48e44be91ba4c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:31:06 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] src: describe the review or the machine, not session codes or
 host names

Comments and docstrings in 11 source files named the review sessions that
measured something (by their codes) or the machines a measurement was made
on (by their host names). Each now says what the reader needs: the review
it came from ("the #1218 review", "review round 3"), or the kind of machine
where it matters ("a Linux cluster", "a 96-thread Linux workstation"). Where
neither matters the attribution is dropped. The H0-H3 matrices in the
adjoint assembly and the A1, B1, C1 and "C1-continuous" names are code and
mathematics, not codes, and are unchanged.

Text only: for every changed file the token stream with comment and string
contents blanked is identical before and after, and for the Python files the
AST with docstrings dropped and strings replaced by a placeholder is too.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
